@startuml sequence_search_expansion_fallback
title Search with expansion: Ollama unavailable or too slow (fallback)

actor Client
participant SearchSocket
participant ThreadPool
participant QueryExpansionService
participant QueryExpansionCache
participant OllamaClient
participant "ollama\n(container)" as Ollama
participant "ollama-recovery\n(daemon thread)" as Recovery
participant ExpandedQuery
participant KeywordSearch
participant Bm25Scorer

Client -> SearchSocket : {"query": "jazz piano"}
activate SearchSocket
note right of SearchSocket: busy flag, parseQuery, requireCurrent\nand the in-flight limit as on the happy path
SearchSocket -> ThreadPool : submit(() -> run(ctx, session, query, built))
deactivate SearchSocket

ThreadPool -> SearchSocket : run(ctx, session, query, built)
activate SearchSocket
SearchSocket -> QueryExpansionService : expand(query)
activate QueryExpansionService
QueryExpansionService -> QueryExpansionCache : get(key)
QueryExpansionCache --> QueryExpansionService : null (not cached)
QueryExpansionService -> OllamaClient : generate(prompt(query))
activate OllamaClient

alt Ollama answers too late
  OllamaClient -> Ollama : POST /api/generate (timeout 5 s)
  Ollama -[#gray]-> OllamaClient : (no answer within 5 s)
  OllamaClient --> QueryExpansionService : throws HttpTimeoutException
else Ollama unreachable
  OllamaClient -[#red]>x Ollama : POST /api/generate
  OllamaClient --> QueryExpansionService : throws ConnectException
else Ollama answers with an error
  OllamaClient -> Ollama : POST /api/generate
  Ollama --> OllamaClient : HTTP 500 or a body without "response"
  OllamaClient --> QueryExpansionService : throws IOException
end
deactivate OllamaClient

QueryExpansionService -> QueryExpansionService : catch (IOException | RuntimeException e)\nLOG.warn("Query expansion failed ...")
note right of QueryExpansionService
  The failure is not cached:
  the next request for this query
  asks Ollama again.
end note
QueryExpansionService -> QueryExpansionService : startRecovery()\nrecovering.compareAndSet(false, true),\nlast start at least RECOVERY_INTERVAL ago\n(RECOVERY_RETRY_INTERVAL after ConnectException)
QueryExpansionService -> Recovery ** : new Thread(..., "ollama-recovery").start()
note right of Recovery
  a failed expansion starts a background
  warm-up (timeout 30 s, at most one per 30 s);
  after a connection failure the next attempt
  is allowed after 2 s
end note
QueryExpansionService --> SearchSocket : List.of()  (no terms, without waiting)
deactivate QueryExpansionService

SearchSocket -> ExpandedQuery : of(query, [])
ExpandedQuery --> SearchSocket : terms jazz 1.0, piano 1.0 only;\nnewTerms() = []
SearchSocket -> Client : {"stage": "query_expansion", "data":\n{"original": "jazz piano", "expanded_terms": []}}

SearchSocket -> KeywordSearch : search(expandedQuery)
activate KeywordSearch
KeywordSearch -> Bm25Scorer : score(query.terms(), query.weights())
note right: only the original terms:\nthe same ranking as POST /api/search
Bm25Scorer --> KeywordSearch : double[] scores
KeywordSearch --> SearchSocket : top 10 results with snippets
deactivate KeywordSearch

SearchSocket -> Client : {"stage": "keyword_search", "data":\n{"results": [...], "time_ms": ...}}
SearchSocket -> SearchSocket : finish(...): session.busy.set(false)
SearchSocket -> Client : {"stage": "done"}
deactivate SearchSocket

group meanwhile, on ollama-recovery
  activate Recovery
  Recovery -> QueryExpansionService : runWarmUp()
  QueryExpansionService -> OllamaClient : generate(prompt("warm up"), 1, WARM_UP_TIMEOUT)
  OllamaClient -> Ollama : POST /api/generate\n{..., options: {temperature: 0, num_predict: 1}}\n(timeout WARM_UP_TIMEOUT = 30 s)
  note right of Ollama: a cold model can finish loading:\nthis client stays connected
  Ollama --> OllamaClient : 200 {"response": ...} (or a failure, logged)
  OllamaClient --> QueryExpansionService : one token
  QueryExpansionService --> Recovery : null or the failure (time logged)
  Recovery -> Recovery : lastRecoveryUnreachable =\nfailure instanceof ConnectException;\nrecovering.set(false)
  deactivate Recovery
end

note over Client, Bm25Scorer
  No error reaches the client: an unavailable Ollama only removes the expansion.
  SearchSocket also catches a RuntimeException from expand() and uses [] (defensive; expand() does not throw).
end note

@enduml
